v/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3d95723dea6e08317f1927be104e51a41a1cf8f9.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 1:49PM MDT until October 23 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is likely with additional rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms expected through Thursday night. The potential for\nflooding impacts continues into Friday.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-10-22T23:19:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 222319 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 519 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered light showers this afternoon and evening. - An uncertain precipitation forecast, but cooler, wetter weather likely returns this weekend. - At least a brief warm-up likely someti